## Layers
1. Hardware  
   - Temperature sensors  
   - Entry sensors (ultrasonic)  
2. Firmware (Arduino IDE)  
   - Read sensors
   - Storing data as class
   - Serialize data 
   - Upload data
3. Connectivity  
   - Wi‑Fi / ESP-NOW
   - Send data to cloud (HTTP)  
4. Cloud  
   - FASTAPI endpoint (Azure lot hub?)

---

## Sensors
- Temperature sensors  
  - Read every few minutes  (_MS variables for config)
  - Send reading to cloud on schedule

- Entry sensors (event-driven)  
  - Detect people/objects passing gate  
  - Trigger recording and upload when event happens

---
## How Temperature sensors works

### senders side
- initialize the Wi‑Fi mode and connecct to recevier
- Read data regularly.
- build data class to store
- Serialize data to byte array
- send the data regularly to recevier

### recevier side
- initialize the Wi‑Fi mode and connecct to senders
- Read data regularly.
- deserialize data
- store data into queue (incompleted)
- build JSON and send HTTP request (incompleted)
- send the data regularly to cloud server (incompleted)


---

## How entry detection works
- Use an ultrasonic sensor that measures distance.  
- The sensor has a baseline distance (example: 20 cm).  
- If something passes and blocks the line, distance becomes smaller (example: 10 cm).  
- The drop in distance means an object is there.  

### detail
- Read distance regularly.  
- Keep a baseline value checking when no one is there.  
- If distance drops below a threshold (or drops by certain amount), mark event start.  
- Wait a few readings to confirm (avoid false trigger).  
- When distance returns near baseline, mark event end.  
- On event end, save timestamps, baseline, min distance, duration, then upload.

## Data upload (incompleted)
- Build a small JSON for data  
- Put data in a queue and send to cloud in background (don’t block sensor loop).  
- If upload fails, retry and keep data in local storage until it succeeds.  

